WEBVTT

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.390
Good morning, Violin.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.660
Good morning, Birdy.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.500
Hey, what's for breakfast?

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.900
You go take a shower first.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.330
Okay!

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.540
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:35.750
<i>Then we repeat, going</i>
<i>eternally round and round</i>

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:43.320
<i>Where will our path lead?</i>

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:49.830
<i>What do I lose sight of when I'm with you?</i>

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:57.500
<i>A colorful array of love and kindness</i>

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:04.170
<i>I've remembered what</i>
<i>I'd forgotten since the days</i>

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:10.450
<i>when we hurt each other over trivial things</i>

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:17.750
<i>The sounds of our footsteps are</i>
<i>the "tracks" that lead to the future</i>

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:25.460
<i>Within the ever-changing scenery... always</i>

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.530
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:32.600
<i>Then we repeat, going</i>
<i>eternally round and round</i>

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:39.640
<i>This melody that paints the future,</i>
<i>until the world changes</i>

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.640
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.880
<i>The sun always rises again,</i>
<i>eternally repeating its arc</i>

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:57.730
<i>It lights up our path</i>

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:45.640
Yang, Nobu, check this out.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.470
What is it, Ross?

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.680
I'm sure she's makin' some money.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.790
We're lucky today.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:59.290
Total jackpot!

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:00.690
Hmm?

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.360
Someone's here.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.790
No problem.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.020
What's the matter?

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.010
It's nothing. They're just some humans.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:42.270
First Rianshel, then Agrazume died too.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:46.840
We can definitely consider ourselves targeted.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.270
What's going on?

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:49.070
I thought...

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:52.940
- that if we disguised ourselves
as natives and hid here, our safety...

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:54.930
- would be guaranteed...

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.880
That's why I gathered you here today.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.120
We don't know what'll happen next.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:06.020
Then doesn't it seem dangerous to stay...

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:09.460
- where that "Dusk" escape man put us?

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:13.230
Maybe we should stick together for a while.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.600
Perhaps not the best idea.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:19.030
There's no guarantee we don't
have a traitor among us, is there?

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:28.080
Just who's targeting us, I wonder?

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.090
Hello.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.830
Yeah, good morning, Shoko.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.500
It's okay, I'm awake.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:51.930
Yeah, I'm off duty today,
but I've got something to do. I'm sorry.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.770
See you later.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.170
"Roppongi District Arisugawa-no-miya
Park Refugee Camp"

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.950
We'll now gather information on the refugee camp.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:13.760
Here at Arisugawa Park, approximately 100 people

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.030
are living lives as refugees.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.630
Where are Hazawa and Masakubo?

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.860
Apparently they're not answering their phones.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:24.370
Aw, man, I don't have time for this.

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:28.200
You said you wanted to investigate this area too!

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.510
True...

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.810
I've never seen a murder with that MO before.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.650
And to cover such distance in an instant like that...

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:39.120
One of our escapees may be an incredible monster.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.680
Ha! Sissy!

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:42.690
Lame-o!

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.120
Space case!

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.290
You're a dirty sissy!

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.120
- Dimwit!
- Hey, listen to those kids!

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.730
Whoa, stop it, you guys!

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:51.560
Cut it out!

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:00.240
It's Marina! Run!

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.670
Hold it!

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:05.370
Y-You'll pay for this!

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:10.480
Don't bully Takumi!
You're cowards who pick on the weak!

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.550
Hey! Hey, stop it!

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:15.380
Don't butt in!

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:22.310
Rough luck, Ryo.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.160
So you two live in this refugee camp.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:32.230
Yup! We've been friends since way before we came here.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:36.340
Marina always helps me out when I'm in trouble.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:39.240
A man being saved by a woman? That's no good.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:43.380
It's better than a man
knocked flat by a woman, isn't it?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.010
What did you say?!

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:50.890
Though as a man, I'd rather
protect a girl than be protected by her.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:52.860
Big talk for you, Chigira.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:55.690
Now, now, it takes all kinds in this world.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.460
What, are you guys doing some kind of mixer party?

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:06.100
Of course not! We came to report on the refugee camp!

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:07.540
Report?

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.470
This way!

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:18.310
I'm happy she's showing us around, but...

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:20.950
You sure she's not just forcing us to play with her?

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:25.990
Well, we can say we're covering
the kids vigorously living at the camp.

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:27.980
Hurry up!

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:29.490
"Temporary Sleeping Quarters Unit 6"

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.260
Ta-da!

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.630
This is where everybody sleeps.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.800
You want to see inside, right?

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:39.070
Marina, no! You can't just
go into other people's tents!

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:40.900
Okay, shall we move on?

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.140
"Bath"

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:51.480
This is the bath. Okay, next!

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:52.910
What, there's more?!

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:57.920
"Shelter for Refugee Animals"

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.690
This is the pet refugee camp.

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.260
This one's cute!
"Shelter for Refugee Animals"

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:02.250
Ow, ow, ow!

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:08.200
"Keep Out"

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.430
Get a move on!
"Keep Out"

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:10.260
"Keep Out"

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:15.500
This is the end of the refugee camp!

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:20.110
The other side of this fence is the Roppongi ruins.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:23.100
Masakubo and Hazawa would've been happy to see it...

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.650
Ruins are so much better than refugee camps!

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.320
We were right to come here instead.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.560
We leave that place to you, Senkawa!

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:35.390
That we do, yessiree!

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.130
Here you go, Takumi.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:43.700
Those kids sure have energy...

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.070
This kind of reminds me of my childhood.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:49.210
I bet you were like that when you were little, too.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:53.340
Yeah, I ran around everywhere with Nataru.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:55.540
I'll bet you were <i>dragging</i> him around.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:59.980
No, I wasn't! We were friends!

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:05.320
I used to get hurt all the time,
and Violin would patch me up.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:08.520
Is "Violin" the person who raised you?

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:13.530
Yeah. She was my caretaker.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:17.030
What's she doing now?

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:19.570
Birdy?

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:21.040
Everybody's looking at you.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.030
Huh?

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:34.680
Thanks. We'll be fine on our own now.

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.390
Tour guide fee.

00:09:36.390 --> 00:09:37.450
You're chargin' us money?!

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:42.120
Obviously! On what planet do people work for free?

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:43.960
You do have a point.

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:48.630
Hey, now, we're not talking
about some kid's pocket money here.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:49.470
You <i>are</i> a kid!

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:53.900
Give me more! Like 5,000 yen! Or 10,000 yen!

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.610
Hey, that's...

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:01.240
Nataru?!

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.250
What's he doing here?

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:06.450
Are you gonna interview
Mr. Shinmyou? I'll introduce you!

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:07.650
W-W-Wait!

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:10.080
You take care of the rest, Senkawa.

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:11.650
Huh, so your high school
journalism club is reporting on the camp.

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:16.650
"Please Don't Touch"
Huh, so your high school
journalism club is reporting on the camp.

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:16.890
Huh, so your high school
journalism club is reporting on the camp.

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:18.260
Er, yes.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:22.770
Mr. Shinmyou is a volunteer who
comes here to give people massages.

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:27.070
I'm not the only volunteer. There are other staff too.

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:29.610
We take turns coming here.

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:31.740
A volunteer, huh?

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:33.730
Introduction fee, please.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:38.670
More!

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:46.290
Hiya, Takumi. Your mom's been looking for you.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:47.920
Let's go, Takumi.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:50.260
I'll be taking this!

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:52.090
What's with her?

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:57.830
Marina and Takumi are always together.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:59.820
They're good, energetic kids, huh?

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:07.010
You might actually call them <i>too</i> energetic...

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:11.850
Watching them reminds me of my own childhood.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:15.320
There was a girl I was close friends with, too.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.850
Bi... Uh, what was she like?

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:22.290
Well, she was energetic, cheerful, and a good girl.

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:26.500
Though she was a bit of a tomboy...

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.630
A tomboy, eh?

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:31.670
Hey! What are you thinking, Tsutomu?!

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:36.210
I'd sure like to know what you were like as a child...

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:39.880
I remember she used to save
me when I was being bullied.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:43.650
We were like Marina and Takumi are now.

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:46.480
And her family was nice, too.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.850
Thanks for the food!

00:11:55.720 --> 00:12:02.930
Birdy, eat slowly! You're shocking Nataru.

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:05.100
But it's so good!

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.000
C'mon, you eat too, Nataru!

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:07.990
Okay.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.870
Thank you for the food.

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:21.050
Don't worry about being polite. Eat up, Nataru.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.680
Thank you.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:31.860
I really liked her and her family.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:36.060
So you still remember Violin...

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:49.110
Wow, we've saved up a lot!

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:52.710
Okay, let's go before Mama and the others catch us!

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:54.110
Those guys...

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.750
Let's get some footage of the ruins, too.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:02.120
Just how do you suggest we get past the fence?

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:03.960
Look over there!

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:09.670
It's dangerous to go over there.

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:13.600
Lots of sketchy folks have
snuck into the Roppongi ruins.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.590
It's dangerous to go inside.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:25.240
Um, would you mind if we
did a short interview with you?

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:30.620
Now this is some nice crumbling!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.250
It's just too awesome!

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:36.090
Huh?

00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:37.860
Get a load of those dangling pipes!

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:38.690
What?

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:46.860
"Marina & Takumi's House"

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.470
We take turns with all the cleaning, too.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:53.380
I'd at least like to move into temporary housing.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:56.110
I lost everything.

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:59.100
But I'll succeed again! I'll...

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:02.780
Well, ain't you guys well off!

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:09.060
Recordin' your fancy-pants video...

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:12.290
Other folks' misfortune must be pretty entertainin'.

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:24.240
Don't take it too much to heart.

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:25.170
Huh?

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.910
What he said.

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:28.380
Right...

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:31.310
You're bein' serious about this, right?

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:37.190
Let's make something good and
show it to lots of people at the festival!

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:39.890
Hey, you're a pretty good guy.

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:42.320
What are you sayin'?

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.830
You still can't find Takumi?

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:51.830
No... I did find some people
who said they saw him with Marina.

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:53.660
Oh dear...

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.770
You seem to be doing better than before.

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:03.750
Yes, I've been feeling so much
better since you started treating me.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:06.280
I'm glad to hear it.

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:09.890
Nataru's a pretty good guy, huh?

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:12.290
He's always been nice.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:17.690
Hayamiya! Where are you guys right...

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:20.530
Hey, are Takumi and his friend with you?

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:21.760
Takumi?

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:23.700
Did something happen?!

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:27.690
He's supposed to move out of the
refugee camp today, but he's missing.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:35.440
So we're going to live here from now on!

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:38.070
Having a bus for a house is pretty cool.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.920
Here's our bed!

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:43.150
And here's the kitchen.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:44.890
Then this is the family room.

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:46.120
That's "living room"!

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:47.620
But there's a folding table.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:49.610
No, this is mahogany!

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:52.490
Aw, it doesn't matter.

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:53.930
Nope.

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:02.740
Let's always live together, okay?

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:05.730
Yeah, I'll stay with you forever.

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:14.980
Have you seen Marina and Takumi?

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:25.360
Did you find them?

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:26.700
No.

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:27.680
Hey...

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.270
- They wouldn't have gone into
the Roppongi ruins, would they?

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:32.530
- They wouldn't have gone into
the Roppongi ruins, would they?
- Ah, those ruins were great!

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:33.970
That was a feast for the eyes!

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:35.670
It's you guys!

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:38.440
Oh, Senkawa and Hayamiya.

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:41.280
Did you see some kids in there?

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:43.680
Like any kids would go in there!

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:50.980
There they are!

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:55.290
So you weren't seeing things.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:57.280
I'll call over a policeman.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.510
Stop struggling, kid!

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.750
Lemme go!

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.740
Please stop! Stop it!

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:30.920
Stop it, you jerk!

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:37.030
How about I break her, too?

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.530
Moron!

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:42.900
Don't you go hurtin' innocent kids.

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:44.530
Poor thing.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:52.040
Young girls like this make us more money.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.890
Oh, I get you!

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.880
Let those children go!

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.260
Mr. Shinmyou!

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:27.280
Oh? You're not dead yet.

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:29.270
You're a stubborn one.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.490
You bastards...

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:51.940
Nataru.

00:18:56.810 --> 00:19:01.650
Get lost, already. From an educational
point of view, your faces are...

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:06.520
Ow!

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:11.420
Sheesh...

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:20.260
Sh-She's a monster...

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:40.990
She's so cool!

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:41.980
Wow...

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:50.120
So you meant to live here all by yourselves?

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:53.740
I'm sorry.

00:19:53.740 --> 00:19:55.470
I want to be with Marina!

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:58.460
I don't want to not be able to see Takumi anymore!

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.210
It'll be okay.

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:06.920
Even if you're separated now,

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:09.720
when you grow up, you'll be
able to see each other for sure.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:11.750
You're lying!

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.190
It's true.

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:21.660
As long as you don't forget your friend,
you're sure to see them again.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.690
So you've saved me again.

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:35.880
Of course. We're friends, after all.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:38.910
But what are you doing here?

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:42.250
My job! Yeah! That's right!

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:44.240
Okay, bye!

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:05.870
Doesn't it seem like this Nataru guy likes you, Birdy?

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:08.740
I like him, too.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:11.650
That's not what I mean...

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:14.580
Have you really never been in love, Birdy?

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.250
"Love," eh?

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:21.090
Like, when your heart flutters or you
think "Oh, I want to see her again"...

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:23.080
"I want to see him again"...

00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:34.670
Well, I might have someone like that.

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:37.410
Huh? Who? What's he like?!

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:39.240
It's a secret.

00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:46.510
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:52.750
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:09.800
<i>If you hang your head like that,</i>
<i>you won't get any sunlight</i>

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:15.340
<i>Look up at the blue sky so you'll grow taller!</i>

00:22:15.340 --> 00:22:21.020
<i>Let's pour a few tears from the watering can</i>

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:27.010
<i>Eventually shoots will spring up</i>
<i>from somewhere in your heart</i>

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.730
<i>Let's take life slowly</i>

00:22:32.730 --> 00:22:37.730
<i>A girl's dreams are neverending</i>

00:22:37.730 --> 00:22:43.970
<i>Ah, there's someone</i>
<i>out there waiting for you</i>

00:22:43.970 --> 00:22:48.810
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:22:48.810 --> 00:22:55.480
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:22:55.480 --> 00:23:00.260
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:23:00.260 --> 00:23:06.250
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:14.270
<i>This is Birdy Cephon Altira.</i>

00:23:14.270 --> 00:23:17.910
<i>Um... In the next episode...</i>

00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:22.440
<i>The investigator me tries to track down</i>
<i>the escapees through the mimesis chips,</i>

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:30.050
<i>but the trail leads her to someone unexpected.</i>

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:34.390
<i>And the alien escapees try to find</i>
<i>the one who's killing their friends...</i>

00:23:34.390 --> 00:23:37.790
<i>Violin, I'm sad!</i>
